8620	{"artifactId":"LLD-733042d2e435fabd-s1","entry":{"id":"review-7b0e133e7295a973f2200042aee58644","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T11:45:04.672Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed option covers the originating Story's complete requirements and acceptance criteria.","evidence":"Repository searches located the LLD and Story s9's documented 50 MiB dependency, but did not locate an independent originating Story record establishing req1–req5 or ac1–ac5. The LLD itself says these criteria were derived and require confirmation. The requested analyzer drill-down did not return a result during this review. [files: docs/standalone/add-optional-output-budget-git-ls-E20261027733042d2/S001/LLD.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S009/LLD.md]","action":"Link the originating Story/request and establish the acceptance baseline so complete intent coverage can be checked.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"git_ls_files currently inherits a 10 MiB limit, rejects truncated successful listings, and the ignore filter currently permits 50 MiB.","evidence":"ls-files.execute calls readGit without a budget and then parseOutput. readGit invokes runShell with { cwd, timeoutMs, signal }; runShell uses 'options.maxBytes ?? DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES', where DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES is 10 * 1024 * 1024. parseOutput rejects stdoutTruncated. createRepoIgnoreFilter uses 'maxBuffer: 50 * 1024 * 1024' and catches failures with a warning and permissive fallback. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/parsers.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/analyze/context/repo-ignore-filter.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The input and helper parameter are new, while runShell already supplies the required configurable byte-budget mechanism.","evidence":"The complete git_ls_files schema contains cwd, paths, cached, others and ignored, without maxBytes. readGit ends with signal?: AbortSignal. ShellOptions already declares 'maxBytes?: number | undefined', and runShell applies it independently to stdout and stderr using raw byte counts. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/shared/utf8-stream.ts]","action":"Reuse runShell as proposed. This scalar option introduces no entity relationships or UX changes requiring companion diagrams.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"There are seven readGit callers other than git_ls_files.","evidence":"Searching readGit( across src finds eight occurrences including the definition: seven production calls total. Besides git_ls_files, the callers are git_ls_tree, git_rev_parse, git_for_each_ref, git_path_history, git_rev_list and git_hash_object: six other callers. Their complete execute bodies were inspected. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-tree.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/for-each-ref.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/path-history.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-list.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/hash-object.ts]","action":"Correct the inventory and invariant to six other callers and enumerate them explicitly in the regression-test plan.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The optional input and trailing helper argument preserve existing calls without a storage migration, while older schemas reject the new input.","evidence":"The existing tool schema has 'additionalProperties: false' and declares an outputSchema, so executeTool validates its input before execution. runShell defaults maxBytes with ??, preserving the existing limit when undefined. The inspected execution path produces ToolResult data and performs no persistent-state writes. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"None; retain the documented requirement that consumers sending maxBytes need an updated daemon.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Providing the git-family budget option leaves the ignore-filter registry migration to Story s9.","evidence":"Story s9 §6 assigns moving the repo ignore filter to its own migration and requires unsupported operations to be reported to the family Story. Its edge-case table explicitly requires the tool budget to preserve the old 50 MB maxBuffer. This design supplies that capability through ls-files/readGit without prescribing a replacement filter implementation. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S009/LLD.md, docs/standalone/add-optional-output-budget-git-ls-E20261027733042d2/S001/LLD.md, src/analyze/context/repo-ignore-filter.ts]","action":"Label repo-ignore-filter.ts in §3 as a future s9 consumer rather than a change site for this Story.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed schema and existing failure pipeline detect invalid budgets, stdout overflow, spawn errors and nonzero exits without returning partial file data.","evidence":"executeTool returns a rejected failure on input-schema mismatch before tool execution. runShell sets stdoutTruncated to 'stdoutBytes > maxBytes'; parseOutput turns that into 'git output was cut at the byte limit' with raw text in failure.original. readGit returns spawnFail for spawnError and fail when code !== 0. ls-files returns either failure before constructing { files }. Exactly-budget output is retained because accumulation uses <= maxBytes. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/parsers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts]","action":"None. Preserve both early failure returns and parseOutput when adding the argument.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every locally stated acceptance criterion ac1–ac5 has a concrete planned test supported by existing test infrastructure.","evidence":"The design maps ac1–ac5 to schema validation, default and raised limits, exact/overflow and Unicode boundaries, unchanged argv/callers/NUL rejection, and coverage integration. installStandInBin supplies a PATH-based executable with call logging; _repo.ts supplies registry registration and temporary repositories. The existing coverage runner exercises git_ls_files through executeTool and asserts its files result; integration tests already cover paths, others and NUL rejection. [files: docs/standalone/add-optional-output-budget-git-ls-E20261027733042d2/S001/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/_bin.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/__tests__/_repo.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/__tests__/git-coverage.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/__tests__/git-tools-integration.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Correct the caller count in the planned regression case. Run schema-rejection cases through executeTool, since direct execute calls bypass executor validation. These are planned tests; their implementation and results have not been verified.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":7,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T11:45:04.672Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
