8651	{"artifactId":"LLD-733042d2e435fabd-s1","entry":{"id":"review-307ddd6adfb7d25bc68e023065f7d99f","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T11:47:23.853Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers all requirements of the originating Story.","evidence":"Searches of docs and .insrc located the LLD and its artifact JSON, but no independent originating Story/request establishing req1–req5 or ac1–ac5. The LLD says: 'The Story record has no acceptance criteria'. Story s9 independently documents the 50 MiB dependency. The analyzer was attempted but did not return before being stopped; direct file inspection continued. [files: docs/standalone/add-optional-output-budget-git-ls-E20261027733042d2/S001/LLD.md, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-733042d2e435fabd-s1.json, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S009/LLD.md]","action":"Link the originating request or Story record and confirm the acceptance baseline before claiming complete coverage.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"git_ls_files currently uses the shell helper's 10 MiB default, while createRepoIgnoreFilter allows 50 MiB.","evidence":"ls-files.execute calls readGit without a budget; readGit calls 'runShell(argv, { cwd, timeoutMs, signal })'. runShell uses 'options.maxBytes ?? DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES', with DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024. createRepoIgnoreFilter uses 'maxBuffer: 50 * 1024 * 1024' and catches failures with a warning and permissive fallback. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/analyze/context/repo-ignore-filter.ts]","action":"Preserve these defaults and keep the consumer migration in s9.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The per-call git_ls_files budget is new, while shell capture limits and truncation rejection can be reused.","evidence":"The existing ls-files schema contains cwd, paths, cached, others and ignored, with no maxBytes. readGit has no budget parameter. ShellOptions already declares 'maxBytes?: number | undefined'; parseOutput rejects stdoutTruncated with 'git output was cut at the byte limit'. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/parsers.ts]","action":"Add only the schema field and helper parameter; reuse the existing shell and parser behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Appending maxBytes after signal preserves the signatures used by all six other readGit callers.","evidence":"Repository search and inspection of all seven calling functions confirm the corrected inventory. ls-tree and rev-parse pass deps?.signal as the fifth argument; for-each-ref, path-history, rev-list and hash-object omit it. None passes a sixth argument. ls-files can pass undefined for signal and the budget as the sixth argument without altering those callers. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-tree.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/for-each-ref.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/path-history.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-list.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/hash-object.ts]","action":"Use the documented positional order. Treat repo-ignore-filter as a future consumer reference, not an implementation change in this Story.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The optional input is additive for existing callers, requires no stored-data migration, and is rejected by an older daemon.","evidence":"The change affects command input and capture options, while output remains the existing {files:string[]} shape. ls-files declares 'additionalProperties: false' and an outputSchema. executeTool validates input before execution for tools declaring outputSchema and returns a rejected failure on invalid input. runShell's nullish default preserves omitted-budget behavior. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Retain additionalProperties:false and the existing output schema. No relationship or persistence change requires an ERD; the prose adequately describes the parameter flow and compatibility.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"This standalone Story supplies the budget capability without taking ownership of s9's ignore-filter migration.","evidence":"Artifact metadata explicitly records 'standalone': true. The migration steps modify readGit, ls-files and tests only. S9's LLD identifies the old 50 MiB maxBuffer as a dependency requiring resolution in the git family; the current ignore filter still calls execFileSync directly. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-733042d2e435fabd-s1.json, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S009/LLD.md, src/analyze/context/repo-ignore-filter.ts]","action":"Keep the registry cutover and permissive-fallback adaptation in s9; clarify the consumer entry in §3 as informational.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed plumbing preserves detectable overflow, invalid-input and git-process failures without returning a partial file listing.","evidence":"runShell counts raw bytes and sets 'stdoutTruncated: stdoutBytes > maxBytes'; onUtf8Data supplies raw.length independently of decoded character count. parseOutput rejects truncation before parsing and puts captured text in failure.original. readGit handles spawn errors and nonzero exits. executeTool validates the proposed integer bounds before tool execution. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/shared/utf8-stream.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/parsers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Preserve this order and test valid NUL-terminated listings at the exact boundary. The ignore-filter fallback described here applies when s9 adopts the tool.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each locally defined acceptance criterion ac1–ac5 maps to a feasible test using existing repository infrastructure.","evidence":"The design maps schema bounds, default/raised budgets, byte boundaries, unchanged callers/argv and coverage to explicit proposed tests. installStandInBin accepts an executable body and records calls; _repo.ts supplies registration and temporary repositories. git-coverage.test.ts already runs an ls-files case through executeTool. The inspected schema snapshot test's GIT_IDS excludes git_ls_files. [files: src/daemon/tools/__tests__/_bin.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/__tests__/_repo.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/__tests__/git-coverage.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/__tests__/git-approval.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-list.ts, docs/standalone/add-optional-output-budget-git-ls-E20261027733042d2/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Implement the mapped tests through executeTool for schema checks. For unchanged callers, assert capture limits separately from result semantics: rev-parse does not reject stdoutTruncated through parseOutput, and rev-list's count branch also bypasses it. These are proposed tests; no implementation tests were run in this review.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":8,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T11:47:23.853Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
