10064	{"artifactId":"LLD-733042d2e435fabd-s1","entry":{"id":"review-cd4c3da0c4e2ff7882edbde59932beaf","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T12:02:39.554Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers all authoritative upstream requirements and the authorized scope extension.","evidence":"Read the revision-3 LLD artifact and associated BUILD/TESTS records. They document the budget feature and added truncation handling, but do not independently establish the originating user answer or an authoritative Story acceptance baseline. The analyzer returned an empty upstream layer. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-733042d2e435fabd-s1.json, docs/standalone/add-optional-output-budget-git-ls-E20261027733042d2/S001/BUILD.md]","action":"Attach the originating request and scope-extension record, and resolve the acceptance-baseline question before approval.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shell default is 10 MiB, ls-files rejects truncated captures, and the existing ignore filter permits 50 MiB.","evidence":"runShell defines 'DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024' and sets 'stdoutTruncated: stdoutBytes > maxBytes'. ls-files calls parseOutput, which rejects that flag. createRepoIgnoreFilter uses execFileSync with 'maxBuffer: 50 * 1024 * 1024' and warns before falling back to permissive behavior. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/parsers.ts, src/analyze/context/repo-ignore-filter.ts]","action":"Retain these behavior descriptions; distinguish the existing execFileSync consumer from its future tool-based migration.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"git_hash_object already always fails when its capture is cut, so the proposed change only clarifies its error message.","evidence":"hash-object reads 'const sha = read.r.stdout.trim()' and checks only the object-name regex. readGit does not reject stdoutTruncated. runShell retains entire decoded chunks while within budget and drops subsequent overflowing chunks. A retained chunk containing a valid SHA followed by dropped output can therefore pass the regex despite stdoutTruncated=true. Truncation does not imply that the retained text is not an object name. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/hash-object.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Describe hash-object's existing behavior as unchecked truncation that may succeed or fail depending on retained output. Include a regression case with a valid retained SHA and later overflowing output.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design can reuse runShell's byte budget and parseOutput's truncation rejection without introducing another capture mechanism.","evidence":"ShellOptions already exposes optional maxBytes, and runShell independently applies it to stdout and stderr. parseOutput accepts a capture plus a parsing callback and rejects truncation before invoking that callback. The current checkout already implements the optional readGit parameter and ls-files field from the earlier build; rev-parse and hash-object still need the proposed parseOutput integration. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/parsers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/hash-object.ts]","action":"Build revision 3 as the remaining parsing changes and tests, preserving the existing budget implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The optional final readGit parameter preserves all six other production callers and their budgets.","evidence":"Repository-wide search found seven production calls plus the definition. Read all seven tool bodies: ls-files supplies the sixth argument; ls-tree, rev-parse, for-each-ref, path-history, rev-list and hash-object supply at most five. readGit conditionally spreads maxBytes only when defined. The analyzer's incomplete caller inventory was supplemented by source search and reads. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-tree.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/for-each-ref.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/path-history.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-list.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/hash-object.ts]","action":"Retain the seven-tool inventory and explicitly preserve rev-parse's deps?.signal when adding parseOutput.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The change is additive at the input boundary, preserves result shapes, and requires no stored-data migration.","evidence":"The inspected tools return transient ToolResult data: files, values or sha. maxBytes is optional, inputSchema retains additionalProperties:false, and readGit defaults through runShell when the parameter is absent. executeTool validates declared input schemas before execution, so an older schema without maxBytes rejects that field. No changed execution path writes stored records. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/hash-object.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Retain the no-rewrite migration and explicit older-daemon rejection behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"This standalone Story changes the shared tool/helper contract while leaving the ignore-filter migration to its consuming Story.","evidence":"The LLD metadata explicitly records 'standalone':true. createRepoIgnoreFilter still owns its execFileSync invocation; the implementation steps do not replace it. The design describes the directed consumer-to-tool-to-helper budget flow and compatibility. This parameter propagation introduces no stored entity relationships or UX changes requiring an ERD or mock. No linked generated companions were supplied for inspection. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-733042d2e435fabd-s1.json, src/analyze/context/repo-ignore-filter.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts]","action":"Clarify that repo-ignore-filter.ts in the call-site list is a future consumer, not a current readGit/tool caller. The existing prose is adequate for this interaction; no additional visual is necessary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Invalid budgets are rejected before command execution, and oversized successful captures can consistently fail without returning data.","evidence":"executeTool calls validateAgainstSchema before tool.execute and returns a rejected failure on invalid input. ls-files declares Type.Integer with minimum 1 and maximum 50*1024*1024. readGit handles spawn/nonzero failures; parseOutput checks stdoutTruncated before parsing and returns a rejected ToolResult without data, retaining captured text in failure.original. Routing rev-parse and hash-object through it supports the proposed failure contract. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/parsers.ts]","action":"Retain the specified handling and preserve readGit failure precedence before parsing. Schema enforcement applies at the executor boundary, not direct execute calls.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each locally defined acceptance criterion ac1–ac6 maps to a suitable planned test.","evidence":"Read git-ls-files-budget.test.ts: it covers schema range, default overflow, complete output between 10 and 50 MiB, exact/one-byte-over boundaries, multibyte names, caller argument preservation and argv/NUL behavior. git-coverage.test.ts includes the schema-field coverage case. The design explicitly maps ac6 to a proposed git-read-cut.test.ts; that file is not yet present, consistent with revision 3 awaiting build. Existing TESTS records establish only the earlier scope, not ac6. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/__tests__/git-ls-files-budget.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/__tests__/git-coverage.test.ts, docs/standalone/add-optional-output-budget-git-ls-E20261027733042d2/S001/TESTS.md, docs/standalone/add-optional-output-budget-git-ls-E20261027733042d2/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Add the ac6 tests, including the valid-SHA-prefix truncation case, and run the git suites and typecheck after implementation. This review inspected test source and records; it did not execute tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":8,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T12:02:39.554Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
