8693	{"artifactId":"LLD-733042d2e435fabd-s1","entry":{"id":"review-ee704097b6665d22db880e62d20ee7eb","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T12:05:17.531Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers every upstream requirement and the authorized scope extension.","evidence":"Located the LLD, build baseline, and adjacent s9 design, but no independent originating Story record or acceptance baseline. The LLD itself says 'The Story record has no acceptance criteria'. The analyzer request returned no bundle during this review. Code supports the proposed mechanism, but cannot establish the complete upstream intent. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-733042d2e435fabd-s1.json, .insrc/build-start/733042d2e435fabd-s1.json]","action":"Attach the originating userValue and scope-extension decision, and establish ac1–ac6 as the acceptance baseline.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The original listing used the default capture budget; rev-parse and hash-object lack truncation checks.","evidence":"Read ls-files and readGit at recorded baseline 55d4a00c6904422f8e40634d0121cab0f0a7925e: readGit calls 'runShell(argv, { cwd, timeoutMs, signal })'. Current rev-parse splits stdout directly; hash-object trims stdout and checks only the object-name regex. runShell retains whole decoded chunks while cumulative bytes fit, supporting the described hash-object success possibility. The budget addition is already implemented in this checkout, consistent with the acknowledged earlier BUILD. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/hash-object.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Treat budget work as already built and the two truncation guards as remaining work.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design can reuse runShell's budget and parseOutput's truncation failure without introducing another capture mechanism.","evidence":"runShell resolves 'options.maxBytes ?? DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES', with DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024. parseOutput checks stdoutTruncated before invoking its parser and returns 'git output was cut at the byte limit'. Both are directly reusable by the proposed tools. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/parsers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/hash-object.ts]","action":"Reuse these helpers and preserve the existing split, trim, and object-name validation behavior for uncut output.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The readGit caller inventory and parameter insertion preserve existing call contracts.","evidence":"Repository search and complete reads of all seven tool implementations confirm the named seven callers. Only ls-files supplies the sixth argument; the other six supply at most signal as argument five. The listed rev-parse and hash-object bodies are precisely the sites needing parseOutput guards. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-tree.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/for-each-ref.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/path-history.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-list.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/hash-object.ts]","action":"Keep the optional budget last and retain the existing per-tool arguments and timeouts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The optional input preserves old requests, rejects unsupported fields on older implementations, and needs no stored-data migration.","evidence":"Baseline ls-files declares additionalProperties:false and no maxBytes. Current implementation adds an optional integer field and conditionally forwards the budget; absent maxBytes still selects runShell's default. executeTool validates input before execution because this tool declares an output schema. The affected functions return transient ToolResults and do not persist records. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Retain the documented older-daemon rejection and the explicit truncation behavior change for rev-parse/hash-object.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"This Story supplies the family-tool capability while leaving the consumer migration to the adjacent Story.","evidence":"The adjacent s9 LLD says to move the ignore filter only when a registry tool expresses its operation and identifies its 50 MB budget as a family-tool dependency. createRepoIgnoreFilter currently calls execFileSync with 'maxBuffer: 50 * 1024 * 1024'. This design adds that capacity without redesigning the filter. The parameter flow is adequately described in prose; no persistent relationship or UX change requires an ERD or mock. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S009/LLD.md, src/analyze/context/repo-ignore-filter.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts]","action":"Keep repo-ignore-filter.ts as a downstream consumer reference, not an implementation change in this Story. No companion rendering is claimed or required for this change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Budget overflow, invalid input, and command failures have detectable failure paths without successful partial listings.","evidence":"runShell sets stdoutTruncated when stdoutBytes > maxBytes, accepting equality. parseOutput rejects that flag before parsing and places raw stdout in failure.original. readGit handles spawn errors and nonzero exits first. executeTool rejects schema-invalid input before execution. createRepoIgnoreFilter catches its current command failure, logs a warning, and returns a permissive filter. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/parsers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/analyze/context/repo-ignore-filter.ts]","action":"Apply parseOutput before splitting rev-parse output or validating hash-object output, as specified; preserve existing command-failure precedence.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each stated acceptance criterion has a concrete, feasible test mapping.","evidence":"Read git-ls-files-budget.test.ts: it covers schema bounds, omitted-budget overflow, larger complete output, exact/over boundaries, multibyte names, six unchanged caller arguments, argv, and NUL rejection. git-coverage.test.ts checks maxBytes and retains the real ls-files coverage case. The design maps ac6 to a new cut-capture suite, including retained valid SHA followed by dropped output. Both stand-in helpers support controlled output. These are design mappings, not evidence that the pending ac6 implementation or tests have passed. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/__tests__/git-ls-files-budget.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/__tests__/git-coverage.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/__tests__/_standin.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/_bin.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/hash-object.ts]","action":"Implement the ac6 suite with staged writes that ensure a valid SHA is retained before an overflowing chunk; run the git suites and typecheck after the remaining changes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":8,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T12:05:17.531Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
